Most important takeaways
	1. CDN: Never stream massive audio files through application servers.
	2. Signed URLs: Securely authorize temporary access to audio.
	3. HLS/DASH: Split audio into chunks and dynamically adjust quality.
	4. Polyglot persistence: Choose databases based on access patterns.
	5. Redis: Cache frequently accessed metadata and recommendations.
	6. Kafka: Decouple playback events from analytics and ML processing.
	7. Batch + Real-time ML: Precompute expensive recommendations and serve them quickly.
	8. Graceful degradation: Playback must remain available even if secondary services fail.
	
Spend the most time explaining the streaming flow, CDN caching, adaptive bitrate streaming and recommendation architecture. Those are the core engineering challenges in designing Spotify.
